        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758312,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo DS, released in 2004, revolutionized handheld gaming with its innovative dual-screen design – a feature reflected in its name, standing for \"Dual Screen.\" This clamshell console, reminiscent of earlier Game Boy models, combined a traditional display with a responsive touchscreen, offering unique gameplay possibilities. Powered by dual processors, it boasted wireless connectivity for local and online multiplayer via the now-defunct Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection. \n\nA commercial success, the DS sold over 154 million units, becoming a cornerstone of Nintendo's lineup and surpassing the Game Boy Advance. Popular titles like *New Super Mario Bros.* captivated players, while its backward compatibility with Game Boy Advance games broadened its appeal. Later models, including the DS Lite and DSi, introduced enhancements like brighter screens, improved battery life, and digital cameras."
          },
